    {
      "id": 56622,
      "name": "dypaca",
      "username": "dypaca",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dypaca/{size}/2079_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-03-26T06:01:23.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Well you don't cancel the effect entirely.&nbsp; If you reveal some but not all of the cards it was searching for, you do apply the effect to them.&nbsp; But just revealing cards does not cause you to shuffle the discard.</p><p>Basically when you are told to reveal cards (either a certain number or until you reveal something), you should act like it also says \"or until you reveal the entire deck\".</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:31:42.694Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
